# Content of the P3 profile files. The first 40 columns are the
# default output from ellipse. From here you can trust geometrical
# parameters like the ellipticity, the position angle, the harmonic
# coefficients, etc. However, for all brightness-related quantities
# such as the intensity at a given isophote, the corresponding surface
# brightness, the accumulated flux or magnitude, etc., you should use
# the P3-specific values at the end. These include the aperture
# corrections that need to be applied on IRAC data (hence the "_COR"
# subscript).

 1  SMA              semi-major axis length (pixel)				 
 2  INTENS           mean isophotal intensity					 
 3  INT_ERR          error in isophotal intensity (RMS / sqrt(NDATA))		 
 4  PIX_VAR          estimate of pixel variance (RMS * sqrt(SAREA))		 
 5  RMS              root-mean-square scatter around isophotal intensity		 
 6  ELLIP            ellipticity							 
 7  ELLIP_ERR        ellipticity error						 
 8  PA               position angle (degrees counterclokwise from +y)		 
 9  PA_ERR           position angle error						 
10  X0               ellipse X center (pixel)					 
11  X0_ERR           error of ellipse X center (pixel)					 
12  Y0               ellipse Y center (pixel)	    
13  Y0_ERR           error of ellipse Y center (pixel)
14  GRAD             local radial intensity gradient				     
15  GRAD_ERR         gradient error						     
16  GRAD_R_ERR       gradient relative error					     
17  RSMA             (semi-major axis length) ** 1/4				     
18  MAG              mean isophotal magnitude					     
19  MAG_LERR         lower magnitude errors				     	 
20  MAG_UERR         upper magnitude errors		 
21  TFLUX_E          total flux enclosed by ellipse			
22  TFLUX_C          total flux enclosed by circle			
23  TMAG_E           total flux enclosed by ellipse, in magnitudes	
24  TMAG_C           total flux enclosed by circle, in magnitudes	
25  NPIX_E           total number of valid pixels inside ellipse	
26  NPIX_C           total number of valid pixels inside circle		 
27  A3               3rd harmonic deviations from ellipse
28  A3_ERR           3rd harmonic deviation errors
29  B3               3rd harmonic deviations from ellipse
30  B3_ERR           3rd harmonic deviation errors         
31  A4               4th harmonic deviations from ellipse	 
32  A4_ERR           4th harmonic deviation errors	 
33  B4               4th harmonic deviations from ellipse	 
34  B4_ERR           4th harmonic deviation errors         
35  NDATA            number of valid data points on isophote			     
36  NFLAG            number of flagged data points on isophote			     
37  NITER            number of iterations					     
38  STOP             stop condition code					     
39  A_BIG            maximum (in abs. value ) among 1st and 2nd                     
40  SAREA            average sector area on isophote (pixel)
#------ P3-specific columns -------
41  REQ              Equivalent radius, sqrt(a*b)                  arcsec
42  NPX              Number of pixels within isophote
43  INTENS_COR       Aperture-corrected intensity along isophote   MJy/str
44  TFLUX_E_COR      Aperture-corrected flux inside isophote       MJy/str
45  SB               Surface brightness                            AB mag/arcsec^2
46  SB_COR           Aperture-corrected surface brightness         AB mag/arcsec^2
47  TMAG             Magnitude inside aperture                     AB mag
48  TMAG_COR         Aperture-corrected magnitude inside aperture  AB mag
49  ESKY             Contribution of the sky to the SB error       MJy/str
50  ETSKY            Contribution of the sky to the TFLUX error    MJy/str
51  PSMA             Radius along semimajor axis                   arcsec
52  ESB              Error in SB                                   AB mag/arcsec^2
53  ESB_COR          Error in SB_COR                               AB mag/arcsec^2
54  ETMAG            Error in TMAG                                 AB mag
55  ETMAG_COR        Error in TMAG_COR                             AB mag
